  "body": "## This relates to...\n\nFixes #6013\n\n## Rationale\n\nSince #5648, `MockAgent` shares a pool's `kDispatches` array with the `${origin}#http1-only` dispatcher that legacy global dispatcher consumers (like Node.js' bundled `fetch`) use. `cleanMocks()` replaced that array, so the `#http1-only` dispatcher kept the old interceptors and never saw new ones.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Features\n\nN/A\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- `MockPool.cleanMocks()` and `MockClient.cleanMocks()` empty the interceptors array in place (and reset its total dispatch count) instead of replacing it, so every dispatcher that shares it sees the change.\n- Tests in `test/node-test/global-dispatcher-version.js` for both, through Node.js' global `fetch`.\n\n### Breaking Changes and Deprecations\n\nN/A\n\n## Status\n\n- [x] I have read and agreed to the [Developer's Certificate of Origin][cert]\n- [x] Tested\n- [ ] Benchmarked (**optional**)\n- [ ] Documented\n- [x] Review ready\n- [ ] In review\n- [ ] Merge ready\n\n[cert]: https://github.com/nodejs/undici/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#developers-certificate-of-origin\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
